result: 'P0-3 verified fixed: generator probe (p31) compiles with no LLVM verifier
  error and yields 0..4 correctly. Pinned via alpha_audit_generator_compiles_and_runs
  asserting exact stdout ''0\n1\n2\n3\n4\n''.'
description: 'The compiler emits LLVM IR that fails LLVM''s own verifier for generator/yield
  lowering. The generator function declares `ptr` return type but emits `ret i64 0`.
  Reproducer: `review/probes2/p31_generator.jn`. Root cause: inconsistent return type
  in `src/codegen/coroutines.rs` or `src/mir/lower/` generator splitting. Fix: align
  the declared LLVM function return type with the actual return value on all paths.
  Add an assertion in the MIR verifier (task 2-26) that catches this at MIR construction.
  Add a test that compiles and runs p31_generator.jn. (review/14_findings.md P0-3,
  review/15_roadmap.md A.3c)'
